{"name":"Copperhead","hex":"#d68755","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Copperhead","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A northerner who sympathized with the South or wanted to end hostilities during the American Civil War.","Any member of the Democratic party. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Copperhead"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eastern copperhead","blocks":[{"text":"The eastern copperhead, also known simply as the copperhead, is a widespread species of venomous snake, a pit viper, endemic to eastern United States of America; it is a member of the subfamily Crotalinae in the family Viperidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Agkistrodon_contortrix_contortrix_CDC-a.png/330px-Agkistrodon_contortrix_contortrix_CDC-a.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_copperhead"},{"title":"Agkistrodon laticinctus","blocks":[{"text":"Agkistrodon laticinctus, commonly known as the broad-banded copperhead, is a venomous pit viper species, formerly considered a subspecies of Agkistrodon contortrix, which is found in the central United States, from Kansas, through Oklahoma and throughout central Texas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Trans-Pecos_Copperhead_%28Agkistrodon_latcinctus_pictigaster%29.jpg/330px-Trans-Pecos_Copperhead_%28Agkistrodon_latcinctus_pictigaster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agkistrodon_laticinctus"},{"title":"Copperhead (politics)","blocks":[{"text":"In the 1860s, the Peace Democrats, also known as Copperheads, were a faction of the Democratic Party in the North who opposed the American Civil War and wanted an immediate peace settlement with the Confederates. Republicans started labeling anti-war Democrats \"Copperheads\" after the eastern copperhead, a species of venomous snake. Those Democrats embraced the moniker, reinterpreting the copper \"head\" as the likeness of Liberty, which they cut from Liberty Head large cent coins and proudly wore as badges. By contrast, Democratic supporters of the war were called War Democrats. Notable Copperheads included two Democratic Congressmen from Ohio: Reps. Clement L. Vallandigham and Alexander Long. Republican prosecutors accused some prominent Copperheads of treason in a series of trials in 1864."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Badge_of_the_Peace_Democrats_%28Copperheads%29.png/330px-Badge_of_the_Peace_Democrats_%28Copperheads%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copperhead_(politics)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg/500px-Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg/1280px-Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg/500px-Copperhead_distribution_%28Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACopperhead_distribution_(Agkistrodon_contortrix_%26_A._laticinctus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Kupferkopf-02.jpg/500px-Kupferkopf-02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_c